{"kind":"assert","text":"R12 integration preparation is read-only and held pending the author's and cost reviewer's ancestry V3 release. The proposed clean base is reviewed R1 de1a0546, tree 29cbdfa14cd52e5d1908d51e27c35c08fc957e33. Immutable Git comparison confirms that de1a adds only the R1 note append after 1793, and that all seven R1 changes since the ancestry author's c59 basis are path-disjoint from the confirmed 22-path ancestry/R2 set. The R12 three new standalone paths and the operator author's seven CLI/test/note paths are also pairwise path-disjoint. No source contents were copied or applied during this inventory.\n\nThe operator author confirms its command depends only on existing authenticated entry/history reads, not a new index or ancestry API. I therefore recommend keeping its source and proof claims in a separate tranche; R12 delivery need not wait on operator CLI integration. A future isolated union should first preserve the complete cleared ancestry/R2 source on de1a as its own checkpoint, then add R12 serving integration as a separate checkpoint. The fixed index lookup/registration, creator/declaration/delivery predicates and original parentless admission stay unchanged; R12 owns separate serving state/method and ingress accounting, not authority. Only the four reviewed counter overrides are proposed, with original adopted defaults and the no-live-eviction 8192 hard capacity. Per-membership verified-key join accounting remains explicitly distinct from deployment-scoped creation/read counters. Actual startup counts, compiler/tests/gate, integration commits and deployment remain unperformed. Root has the exact overlap inventory and minimum-tranche recommendation.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}